plugin-hostd (0.14.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Version 0.14.0: the probe's SCHED_FIFO measurement (#225) in the spec's
    changelog
  * Version 0.14.0: the probe's SCHED_FIFO measurement (#225, #235) in the
    changelogs
  * Version 0.14.0: estimate, core placement, the wire protocol document, the
    Zynthian chain tools and docs
  * docs/zynthian: omx-eq8 retaken on omx-plugins 0.16.0: the add is refused
    on a stale pin, mod-ui no longer crashes
  * probe: the lock preload's default is where make install puts it, and the
    packages build with their PREFIX (#225)
  * probe tests: the capability-drop arm fails, not skips, without a user
    namespace under PROBE_REQUIRE_REALTIME (#225)
  * probe: CAP_SYS_NICE counts only in the initial user namespace, so a
    namespace keeps its rlimit grant (#225)
  * docs/zynthian: README names the captures page
  * docs/zynthian: captures of the generated menus, the MOD GUIs and the
    plugin figures on the Pi 5
  * probe tests: the refusal arm grants itself an rlimit where it holds
    CAP_SYS_RESOURCE (#225)
  * evidence: placement none against spread on a Pi 5, two and three
    instruments (#226)
  * zynthian image: quote the jack2 failure as the log has it
  * zynthian image: the first boot under qemu-system-aarch64, step by step
  * zynthian image: boot the image in a container and record what that proves
  * protocol-doc: estimate in the chains and plans group, and
    docs/protocol.md written again
  * protocol-doc: estimate in the chains and plans group, and
    docs/protocol.md written again
  * bench, tools/zynthian: read a worker_list record with or without its core
  * docs/zynthian/benchmarks.md: grouped versus alone at 16 chains, from the
    stress run
  * site: docs/placement.md in the reference section
  * protocol-doc: estimate is a verb of pins and qualification;
    docs/protocol.md written again
  * docs/zynthian: the Pi 5 stress run, grouped versus alone versus jalv,
    with its data and captures
  * stress-figures.py: one table and one set of figures from several runs,
    each mode from the last run that holds it
  * CI: the RPM's file list carries the probe's lock preload (#225)
  * CI: the probe's highest priority comes from an rlimit the test raises,
    not from CAP_SYS_NICE (#225)
  * placement: one worker per chain or isolated plugin, pinned across the
    audio cores (#226)
  * tests: core placement across the audio cores, and its sabotage (#226)
  * docs/zynthian: instruments through the engine, Surge XT on the Pi 5
  * tools/zynthian: play an instrument and measure what it gives back
  * tools/zynthian: the stress run reads CPU from the scheduler's ns
    counters, not the tick
  * docs: core placement, one worker per chain pinned across the audio cores
    (#226)
  * probe lock preload: no dead store when the report cannot be written (#225)
  * probe tests: raise the limits with CAP_SYS_RESOURCE, and in CI never skip
    a real-time arm (#225)
  * probe: the lock is bounded by the RLIMIT_MEMLOCK hard limit, not the
    memory limit (#225)
  * probe: a missing lock preload is the reason before a small RLIMIT_MEMLOCK
    (#225)
  * probe: a child holds no CAP_SYS_NICE past its exec (#225)
  * docs: the manual's shape in docs/site.yml, a landing page for Zynthian,
    Start here and How to contribute
  * tools/site: the site as a manual, shaped by docs/site.yml
  * probe: a describe, a panel or a pin pass keeps the runner's
    RLIMIT_MEMLOCK and RLIMIT_RTTIME (#225)
  * estimate: a chain's latency, CPU, RAM and workers from the records
  * supervisor: what the planner is told of a plugin, read by its uri
  * qualcost: read the cost median and the latency of one grid point
  * CI: the test container holds CAP_SYS_NICE, so the probe's
    highest-priority arm runs (#225)
  * docs: the probe measures at real-time priority, and how a service grants
    it (#225)
  * probe: run --list-limits prints the bounds a run would apply here (#225)
  * probe: the measurement runs SCHED_FIFO at the highest priority granted,
    memory locked (#225)
  * tools/zynthian: the Pi 5 stress run, chains of 4 at 1 to 16 chains,
    grouped, alone and on jalv
  * probe: a lock preload that locks the measured child's memory (#225)
  * probe output 1.2: the measurement's real-time class and memory lock,
    declared (#225)
  * ci: the zynthian-chain job reads the spike's patch before the round
    trip's namespace
  * docs/index.md: the Zynthian use case, its pages listed as coming until
    each is published
  * docs/zynthian: the upstream patch series, step by step, each with its
    base and proof
  * image-build.sh: the sbin tools on PATH, and a command the update cannot
    find fails the build
  * tools/zynthian: the matrix starts only after another lane's stress run on
    the device
  * docs/zynthian: the image with our work, how it is built and checked
  * docs/zynthian: the Pi counts in three classes, suitable, isolated and
    unsuitable
  * docs/zynthian: the benchmarks, the trade-offs and the acceptance report,
    for the upstream review
  * docs/zynthian/evidence: the Pi 5 bench runs of 2026-10-27 and 2026-10-28
    and the qualification summary
  * tools/zynthian: the qualification summary, the figures, and the benchmark
    matrix runner
  * bench/report: qualification records count verdicts, one per host profile,
    not plugins
  * bench: each row counts the JACK clients its host put on the graph
  * docs: the wire protocol, generated from the protocol data and checked in
