  * docs/zynthian: the Path A verb table, as devel/zynthian holds it
  * tools/zynthian: image-build.sh updates upstream's vangelis image with the
    forks and OpenMixer
  * image-inspect.sh: the OpenMixer packages and each repository's remote URL
  * docs: a landing page, and the pages workflow that publishes the site on
    GitHub Pages
  * tools/site: render docs/ into a static site, with the figures and
    captures its pages reference
  * chain-e2e.sh: the spike engine's patch read before the network namespace,
    which has no network
  * docs/zynthian: the engine lives in the FreeMixer/zynthian-ui fork, and
    the spike's patch leaves the tree
  * tools/zynthian: the spike's engine read from the commit it was last
    changed at, by spike-engine.sh
  * CI: bench.yml runs the report writer's unit tests
  * Report: the governor of a hand run is read from that run's own file
  * Report: a partial run (missing host, rate, frames or plugin cell) is
    reported as partial in the document and fails --strict
  * Report: read latency_frames and the per-row stress field the bench
    writes; order run ids by number; test on the shipped example document
  * Report tool: no default under HOME; every input is an argument,
    documented in --help
  * Report --strict: validate first, write nothing when it fails, give the
    reasons on stderr
  * Report: a missing key is a validation error naming the key and the file;
    no fallback substitutes a value
  * Report facts: every source is a public pull request; the device, file
    count and command come from the run's own document
  * Report: sections 1, 2, 5 and 6 restate public pull requests line by line;
    the unmeasured product claims are gone
  * Bench: a script that writes the Zynthian acceptance report from
    measurement files
  * Design note: generate what a plugin lacks for Zynthian, never touch its
    own bundle (#218)
  * fuzz: the mutant records follow the moved lines of src/verbs.c (#174)
  * verbs: the omx-clap-core header is the render of omx-clap-core-contract
